  "answer_text": "It looks like you may be referring to **Iuka, Mississippi** (sometimes misspelled as \"Luka\"). Here's an overview:\n\n### Iuka, Mississippi\n\n- **Iuka** (pronounced /a\u026a\u02c8ju\u02d0k\u0259/) is a city in and the county seat of **Tishomingo County, Mississippi**, United States.\n\n- Its population was **3,139** at the 2020 census, and **Woodall Mountain**, the highest point in Mississippi, is located just south of Iuka.\n\n- Iuka is built on the site of a Chickasaw village, and the name \"Iuka\" comes from the name of one of the chiefs of that village.\n\n- Iuka was founded by David Hubbard, a wagon train scout, and Euro-American settlers arrived with the Memphis and Charleston Railroad in 1857.\n\n- The Civil War brought widespread devastation when a major engagement occurred on September 19, 1862 \u2014 the **Battle of Iuka** \u2014 resulting in 1,200 to 1,500 killed or wounded.\n\n- Iuka is located in **northeast Mississippi**, with U.S. Route 72 running through the southern part of the city.\n\n- Six artesian springs flow to the surface in Iuka at **Iuka Springs Park**, though currently only three springs are still flowing.\n\nCould you clarify what specifically you'd like to know about Iuka/Luka, Mississippi? For example, its history, attractions, or something else?",
